# The room scene, which F7 in mygame cycles to: a room built by hand as a mesh file, meshes/room.mesh, with white
# walls, a checker floor, a red pillar and a green partition, lit by a quad light under the ceiling (see
# docs/content/kinds/meshes.md#mesh-files). The room's mesh is its collider too, and three boxes fall onto its floor when
# the world runs (see docs/physics/design.md#shapes). A reflection probe's box reaches past the walls, so its fade ends
# outside them, and its projection box is the walls', which lines the floor's reflections up with them (see
# docs/rendering/lighting-and-shadows.md#reflection-probes). On the floor, a mirror and a panel of brushed metal show the
# screen-space reflections from the Medium quality up, sharp on the mirror and blurred by the panel's roughness, and the
# probe where the screen has nothing to show (see docs/rendering/lighting-and-shadows.md#screen-space-reflections). The
# camera stands inside, near the front wall. Positions are raw World_Position values in units of 2^-24 m. The editor
# writes this file; see docs/editor/document-and-scenes.md#scenes.
